==================================================================================
PARITY (web FeedbackModal.tsx -> native), no scope narrowing
==================================================================================
  Data sources (web -> native P1/S8 seam):
    useTranslation              -> FeedbackStrings facade (P1/S10), no literals.
    useSubmitFeedback           -> FeedbackSubmitting.submit(_:) async (POST
                                   /feedback), drives in-flight + failure state.
    useLocation / navigator /   -> FeedbackContextSource resolves FeedbackContext
      import.meta.env / error-     (pageRoute + appVersion + client identity +
      Reporter ring + console      recentErrors[] + consoleTail), source-owned.
  Composition (web Modal/form -> native):
    Modal "Report a bug / Send  -> header title + freshness chip + close "x".
      feedback"
    Select category (bug/feature-> FeedbackCategorySelector (menu Picker, glyph +
      /other)                      label per option, accessibilityLabel).
    Input Title (5..120)        -> FeedbackTextField (cap 120, blur via FocusState
                                   marks touched, inline zod-parity error).
    Textarea Details (20..4000) -> FeedbackTextArea (TextEditor, cap 4000, blur,
                                   inline error, prompt overlay).
    Auto-attached context box   -> FeedbackContextPanel (phase-switched) + rows
                                   Page/App version/Browser (Browser key kept for
                                   parity; value = native client identity) +
                                   2 toggles (recent errors ON, console OFF) +
                                   HelperText each.
    submit.isError role=alert   -> FeedbackSubmitErrorAlert.
    Button ghost Cancel         -> TSButton(.ghost) -> onClose (disabled while
                                   submitting, web disabled={isSubmitting}).
    Button primary Send (disabled-> TSButton(.primary) .disabled(submitDisabled);
      until valid; "Submitting...") label swaps to "Submitting..." in flight.
    onSubmit payload assembly   -> FeedbackProjection.submission: trims title+body,
      (trim + conditional          attaches recent_errors only when toggle ON AND
      recent_errors/console_tail)  count>0, console_tail only when toggle ON AND
                                   the last-4000-char tail is non-empty.
    close-on-success reset       -> model.submit() resets fields on success; the
      (web useEffect(!open))       view dismisses only when submit succeeded.
  Tailwind classes were NOT ported; chrome is P1/S9 tokens (TSSpacing/TSRadius/
  Color.TS/Font.TS) via TSGlassPanel/TSFadeIn/TSButton.

==================================================================================
STATES (every state renders — no hidden surfaces)
==================================================================================
  loading  -> FeedbackContextLoadingState (skeleton rows + spinner + "Gathering
              diagnostics...") in the auto-context panel; the form renders at once
              (web parity — the web form is instant; only diagnostics are gathered).
  empty    -> FeedbackContextEmptyState (ContentUnavailableView "No diagnostic
              context available") — diagnostics resolved with nothing to attach.
  error    -> FeedbackContextErrorState (QueryError-equivalent + Retry ->
              model.retryContext()).
  stale    -> freshness chip "Stale" + connectivity banner + ONE guarded auto-
              refresh (re-armed on return to live).
  offline  -> freshness chip "Offline" + banner; cached context kept; no refetch.
  content  -> the populated context rows + toggles (+ inline reload error if a
              refresh failed while a cached context remains).
  submit   -> in-flight "Submitting..." (disabled) + post-failure inline alert.
  Telemetry: model.start() emits P1/S11 view.opened surface="FeedbackModal" (once,
  idempotent — ModelTests proven).

